<meta>
<title | A Body-Content Article for JATS Export>
<author | Test Author>
<abstract |
This abstract has *italic* and **bold** and `inline code` interleaved
with prose to verify the slice 5b paragraph-grouping fix.
>
</meta>

<section sec-type=lists | Lists>

An unordered list:

<list>
<li> First item with *emphasis*.
<li> Second item.
</list>

An ordered list:

<list ordered>
<li> One
<li> Two
</list>

A definition list:

<dl>
<dt | term-A>
<dd | Definition A with prose.>
<dt | term-B>
<dd | Definition B.>
</dl>

<section | Math>

Inline math <$ E = mc^2 $> in a paragraph, with ~~a struck-out aside~~.

A numbered display equation:

<$$ #eqn:euler | e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0 $$>

An align environment with two lines:

<align>
a^2 + b^2 &= c^2 \\
x + y &= z
</align>

<section | Theorem family>

<theorem name="Pythagoras" #thm:pyth | If $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$ then the triangle is right-angled.>

<proof | By similar triangles. ∎>

<section | Links>

External links export as ext-link, e.g. <a href="https://example.org/spec" | an external spec>; an internal link to a fragment id exports as a cross-reference, e.g. <a href="#thm:pyth" | the Pythagoras theorem>.

<section | Frameables>

<fig #fig:elephant src=elephant.jpg | An elephant.>

<table #tab:demo csv caption="A small CSV table.">
a,b,c
1,2,3
</table>

<aside type=warning title="Heads up" caption="See the calibration log." | Always calibrate the instrument first.>
